 false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "Deepak sold a bike to Sharath at a profit of 40%. Sharath sold his bike to Sivaji at a loss of 30%. If Deepak paid ₹8,000 for this bike, then find the cost price of the bike for Sivaji.", "options": [{"text": "₹6,728", "added": false}, {"text": "₹7,840", "added": false}, {"text": "₹5,423", "added": false}, {"text": "₹11,200", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "successive-transactions", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "The marked price of a book is ₹767. A shopkeeper allows a discount of 20% and still earns a profit of 30%. Find the cost price of the book (in ₹).", "options": [{"text": "680", "added": false}, {"text": "450", "added": false}, {"text": "472", "added": false}, {"text": "525", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "basic-cp-sp", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "P aims to get total 360 marks out of 500. He gets 5% less than his target. How much does he get?", "options": [{"text": "335", "added": false}, {"text": "325", "added": false}, {"text": "340", "added": false}, {"text": "330", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "If A and B together can complete a work in 15 days, B and C together in 12 days and C and A together in 10 days, then in how many days can B alone complete the work?", "options": [{"text": "30", "added": false}, {"text": "45", "added": false}, {"text": "35", "added": false}, {"text": "40", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}]}